[Music]  hello and welcome to drive at the DW car  show on this edition a world premiere in  Barcelona  od unveils its new a8 taking the plunge  the MP car 770 plus the new e-class  convertible from Mercedes  [Music]  the new e-class convertible rounds off  mercedes-benz e-class range it's the  fifth member of the family alongside the  sedan the station wagon the coupe a and  all terrain models and it could look  back in a very successful history dad a  300 C e24 from 1992 was mercedes-benz  first four-seater convertible explains  our car man Emmanuelle and even back  then it boasted some rather special  safety features like the automatically  deployed robot the new model has it too  many other things  hi [ __ ] male among the standard  features are a driver fatigue attention  assist an active brake assist and the  pre-safe system familiar from other  models which can prevent accidents by  identifying critical handling situations  plus multi-beam LED headlights ensure  the road ahead is always clearly visible  after dark the designers also set out to  increase pedestrian safety in case of a  head-on collision and certain  circumstances the rear section of the  hood can be lifted up the increased  clearance from the components in the  engine compartment creates additional  deformation space to reduce the risk of  injury to pedestrians  the LED tail lights featuring a new  crystal treatment are likewise standard  the optional comfort package creates an  in-car Indian summer thanks to the air  scarf neck level heating and the air cap  feature which cuts down air turbulence  we checked out the e 400 convertible  with a 245 kilowatt engine the interior  shows the usual high quality workmanship  and equipment it's replete with leather  and high gloss finishes and there's a  range of extras to make driving more  enjoyable there's a heated steering  wheel and for the front seats a memory  function and ventilation to keep you  cool when the weather's hot there's  something for everyone here the standard  fitted acoustic soft top which minimizes  noise and enhances climate comfort opens  and closes in 20 seconds  [Music]  and that also applies when you're on the  road of course up to a speed of 50 km/h  as every convertible driver knows  explains him on well when the car has  been parked in the Sun for a few hours  leather seats can be pretty  uncomfortable especially if you're  wearing shorts so Mercedes came up with  heat reflecting leather it keeps the  temperature reasonable so when the car  has been standing in the Sun you're not  likely to burn your legs the e-class  convertible offers a range of five  gasoline and diesel engines with the Eco  start/stop function the three liter  6-cylinder unit we had propelled our  test car from zero to 100 km/h in 5.5  seconds top speed is 250 emanuelle finds  the engine output range from 143 to 245  kilowatts pretty impressive even the  smallest unit packs a punch  plus the 9g tronic automatic  transmission is standard for all and all  wheel drive is also optionally available  and the new model is big the convertible  is 12 centimeters longer 7 centimetres  wider and has an 11 centimeter longer  wheelbase than its predecessor overall  Amano says the new e-class convertible  is a perfect open top four seater the  simple reason is there is no real  competition in this segment and this is  no 1 of the 4 seater this is the unique  article as rear seat passengers will  discover two  [Music]  [Applause]  prices started just over 54,000 euros in  Germany with the e 400 we tested costing  70 thousand euros plus car makers are  always conjuring up new ways of  presenting their products welcome to the  inaugural edition of the Audi summit  where the Bavarian showcase the  innovations they hope will make them a  premium digital car company at trade  fairs today says sales and marketing  chief deep mouthful tonight new products  are just a mouse-click away you can  present a car at the fair and post the  complete presentation online trade fairs  no longer have quite the same status so  we thought it would be a good idea to  make a strong branding statement now and  again and that Audi summit was born it  was an explosive showcase of the Audi  range if you've got it flaunt it  the huge mainstage played host to an  extravaganza of dance acrobatics and  automotive ballet the highlight of the  audiovisual spectacular the world  premiere the new flagship a8 now in its  fourth generation over 2,000 guests from  around the world we're in Barcelona to  witness the event welcome to the Future  Premium welcome to the all-new Audi a8  the challenge explains Audi design chief  mark least it was to introduce a new  design theme and it makes sense to start  with a top-of-the-range model you can  see how the a8 has a completely new  exterior look the shoulder line has been  lowered to between the wheels that  created more space for muscles above the  front and rear wheels and that new  design vocabulary makes the a8 highly  distinctive all over the exterior  whether on the sides the rear at the  front the single frame radiator grille  has undergone some radical changes mike  leake this is the single frame now has  significantly different proportions for  the last 10 years it was more vertical  so to visualize the performance  character they made the grille flatter  and wider inside out he wanted to up the  comfort with plenty of space for rear  passengers - and there are some  interesting new features up front  building touch screens that let the  driver operate the a8 in smartphone  style the architecture the dashboard is  all new like no other howdy before it is  smooth now we've integrated the displays  into a piano black finish fleshing to  github and as for what those controls  can do the new a8 is the world's first  production car with advanced autonomous  driving technology and slow moving  traffic on highways it can take control  of the car at speeds of up to 60 km/h  allowing the driver to focus another  another highlight is the active  suspension a front-mounted camera and  laser scanners detect uneven patches of  road in advance and adjust the  suspension accordingly  the electromechanical rotary damper  system responds in milliseconds and  adapts to the road conditions the new  Audi a8 also absorbs the kinetic energy  generated by any bumps or holes ensuring  a very smooth ride  [Music]  and the new luxury sedan is also setting  the pace on the safety front an array of  cameras ultra scan sensors and radar and  laser scanners combined to prevent  collisions the car analyzes the driving  behavior of other vehicles passenger  safety is top priority  the first new a8 models to hit the road  come with a v6 gasoline engine and a v6  diesel they will be followed by eight  and twelve cylinder versions and a  plug-in hybrid  Jaguar has launched its new compact SUV  with a spectacular stunt the e pace  dually leaped into the Guinness Book of  Records with a 270 degree barrel roll  the new crossover comes with a choice of  three diesel and two gasoline engines  it's a step down in size from the F pace  and in price to starting at just under  35,000 euros in Germany Ford is  presenting the new generation of the  Fiesta the iconic supermini celebrated  its 40th birthday last year but it's  looking younger and more progressive  than ever before it will come in seven  equipment lines with a range of  customization options and spring 2018  sees the arrival of the fiestas active a  crossover model featuring higher ground  clearance and protective cladding  [Music]  car tester undelete Zimmerman recalls  Subaru rolling out its very first  rear-wheel drive vehicle in 2012 the  result of a collaboration with Toyota  it was named rather unimaginative li  boxer rear-wheel drive Zenith or BRZ and  now he'd like to find out what makes  this rear wheel drive car with a boxer  engine a Zenith of automotive  achievement the BRZ and the identical GT  86 by Toyota were the first product of  Subaru and Toyotas collaboration Subaru  had taken the initiative and then Toyota  expressed its interest and adding the  sports car to its model range the moment  Andre steps on the gas he realizes the  engine is not the reason for the  confident name especially not in  combination with the automatic  transmission but that's only half the  story under the hood the Toyota  influence is obvious the boxer engine  combines natural aspiration with Toyotas  d-4s direct injection  the Mystics more important to Andre then  the performance of this engine is the  construction type is a boxer engine  that means the crankshaft and the  cylinders are in this case above level  with the tops of the tires but as we  don't have an inline four-cylinder  configuration so the center of gravity  is farther back that allows a near ideal  distribution of weight with a low center  of gravity the BR C's facelift has left  the basic body completely intact  what's new are the full LED headlights  reworked from fasciae and restyled rims  the racy contours accompanied by flared  rear fenders impress sports car fans  from the outset the new rear spoiler now  stands some distance above the trunk lid  the taillights have also been reworked  [Music]  the spring rates for the suspension and  the dampers have been tweaked and the  rear stabilizers reinforced in Andrzej  notices that high centrifugal forces  hardly bothered the BRZ this is where  Subaru shows it's true cornering  qualities the suspension is very  communicative and dynamic the driver  always knows what the front and rear  axles are doing and where there's any  loss of traction so they can respond  instantaneously blitz Noda again our  test car had the sports plus line which  differs from the regular sports edition  only thanks to the Alcantara leather and  heated seats the six-speed automatic  transmission in this car is great at  saving fuel since it tends to rain in  both the acceleration and the top speed  the vrc's tires are the same size as the  ones on the current Toyota Prius so the  BRC might drift a bit rather than  keeping to its lane amateur racing  drivers often replace them with  something that has a bit more traction  notice is how dynamic the Subaru can be  when accelerating out of a curve a  differential lock sensitive to the  torque make sure the thrust goes to the  wheel with the most traction so it's not  wasted the BRZ is a driving machine a  samurai that cuts its way through curves  the engine may not be that powerful but  the car has still become very popular as  a sports coupe a due mainly to its  excellent handling even so most buyers  up for the BRZ twin from Toyota and its  lower price tag  [Music]  venez concept under assure that anyone  who understands the vrc's concept will  agree it's a curved monster of the  highest quality anybody who doesn't like  that would probably rather drive  straight than around bends but andre  still wouldn't call it the zenith the  rear wheel drive boxer engine cars  Porsches had a monopoly claim to that  for decades one last tip don't buy the  automatic buy this stick shift  here to Porsche is years ahead of Subaru  when it comes to rapid-fire  automatic shifting angle front lip  sticks convinced that when it comes to  towing capacity there's just no way  around the Volkswagen Touareg it can  handle up to 3.5 tonnes but he's going  to concentrate on the interior because  this is a special Turek the interior has  some juicy details in store VW had some  new ideas for the Touareg facelift aside  from the new front section the changes  to the exterior are hard to spot  taking center stage among the  innovations are the v6 TDI engines  they've acquired an SCR catalytic  converter module that considerably  reduces nitrogen oxides the driver can  indulge in the torque to cruise along or  put on the power it makes the dash to  100 km/h in 7.3 seconds reaching a top  speed of 225 kilometers per hour  VW has also given its workhorses  taillights a new grooming  cargo capacity begins at 697 liters with  a maximum of 1642 liters the trailer  hitch pops out at the push of a button  [Music]  the Triggs air suspension carries it  across the roughest terrain on top of  the sporty our line design on the  outside our test car had the extensive  executive package of interior features  home Bruni is impressed the nappa  leather seats have the diamond quilted  pattern and decorative stitching Plus  adjustable heating and ventilation the  dash has luxurious woodgrain trim but  one thing that shows the spiffed up  Tuareg is in cutting edge in every  respect is the relatively sluggish  infotainment system the steering tool  feels a bit indirect on the road that  has to do with making it suitable for  off-road maneuvering even so the power  steering makes parking for example a  cinch and physical terms  [Music]  if all we talk Bharani VW Touareg is a  midsize luxury SUV chock full of luxury  features thanks to the air suspension he  can lower the rear at the push of a  button handy for loading heavy objects  it may take a little while but it works  like a charm the Touareg is a great  all-rounder for car buyers with the  necessary financial resources it can  handle rugged terrain heavy loads and  even families out on vacation today our  classy car expert christophe Bauer is  hitting the road in a unique mix of  color and boat it's German engineers  Hans triples legendary MP car as early  as 1932 the self-taught automotive  designer had converted his old dkw race  car into an amphibious vehicle but his  most important creation was the Amphicar  770 produced starting in 1961 it was the  first series production amphibious  vehicle made for private customers hunts  Christoph says banks triple was obsessed  with creating an amphibious car and  devoted his entire life to the idea the  Christoph says The Passion of visionary  did experience some setbacks like in  December 1934 when the car ended up at  the bottom of the Rhine River during a  test-drive  but that very night triple salvaged his  waterlogged vehicle and three days later  it was back on the road through all the  highs and lows he never let anything  distract him from his vision Triple  built his last amphibious car prototype  in 1990 at the age of 81 series  production of the MP car began in 1961  Hannes tipple got financing from German  industrialist habit quant the amphibious  car mainly targeted the US market which  as Christophe notes was evident from his  very name  as neckla Nelson he explains it was  called the 770 because it could go  around seven miles per hour in water and  70 miles per hour on land he thinks the  car is a great idea and should have sold  like hotcakes in the land of opportunity  the amphicars body was made in the  northern German city of Lubeck with the  final assembly being done in Berlin  production of 25,000 EFI cars was  planned but the initial reaction to the  model was less than enthusiastic  [Applause]  [Music]  yeah I'm fika Christoph quotes one of  the first damning verdicts the Amphicar  combines the qualities of an impractical  car with those of an impractical  motorboat  he says that's cruel but unfortunately  true he hasn't tried it in water yet but  even on land driving down winding roads  is enough to make you seasick the little  1.1 litre rear-mounted engine from  triumph delivers just 38 horsepower  which doesn't make for much driving  pleasure and back in 1961 the Americans  with their big v8 engines were used to  something else entirely  about a man still the Amphicar is a real  beauty huh okay that was a joke  Christopher he thinks that the designs  overly ambitious though well intended it  looks half-baked he admits there's some  nice chrome trim and of course these  generous tail fins as a nod to us  customers the fins also serve to break  any waves and protect the engine from  getting flooded the amphibious part  these two ships propellers down here  that drive the car in the water the  bottom part of the body is a completely  sealed hole and here in the doors there  are extra rubber seals to keep the water  out at least that was the hope Topsy  couldn't before the Amphicar was  delivered to buyers every single one was  tested in a pool first to make sure it  was watertight still one look at the  Afrikaners standard equipment its water  breaking tail fins raised exhaust pipe  and obligatory paddle doesn't exactly  fill Christoph with confidence  [Music]  ripped-up will it float or won't it  fatzkee wonders now comes the exciting  part here we go it's very important to  insert the navigation light here at the  rear especially when traveling at night  then Christa gets in and battens down  the hatches these little levers on the  doors are to seal everything off  completely it's time to head for the  water once he's in he'll put it in  neutral and engage the propellers using  this stick shift  fair winds and following seas  Oh God he says it's a strange feeling  driving a car into the water it's  floating it's floating christophe simply  can't believe it driving by it's two  ships propellers the Amphicar can  achieve a speed of 6.5 knots or roughly  12 kilometers an hour the propellers  have to be switched off as soon as it's  back on dry land without the counter  pressure of the water they'd rotate far  too fast and cause massive damage to the  separate water transmission  [Music]  Kristof honestly can't understand why  you need a sport boat license to pilot  the Amphicar in Germany because it's  hardly a sporty mode of transport  churning along so casually just turning  it takes a lot of patience because the  steering only functions through the  front wheels and the turning circle is a  whopping 35 metres though salt water  could be corrosive the Amphicar is even  seaworthy in 1962 for Britain's crossed  the English Channel in 2 MP cars that  took them just under 7 and a half hours  getting into the water isn't a problem  but getting out can be the 770 is a  rear-wheel drive model so the front  wheels are of no help when it comes to  navigating steep shorelines  [Music]  Christophe says the vehicles pretty high  maintenance - after five hours in the  water there are a dozen spots that need  greasing and that's not his thing in the  1960s most potential buyers were the  same opinion of the twenty five thousand  vehicles planned just three thousand 878  were actually built and production  ceased altogether in 1968 only a few  Americans bought one but Krista thinks  that's a real shame because as the first  series production amphibious vehicle for  private use  the Amphicar is definitely a milestone  and automotive history and great fun -  at first Christoph laughed at the  Amphicar but in the end he wanted one  himself  no wonder the model is prized by  collectors and commands high prices MP  cars in good shape can change hands for  well over 50,000 euros and next time on  driving the new Audi rs5 coupe a  [Music]  and be afraid be very afraid the  rolls-royce wrath black patch  [Music]

